sh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"c4e8d9dfe957d32585de2dd5477b79cc11ee7c64667c960c3b6e3ca0891e34cb","event_uuid":"5c57b26c-7682-49df-ad64-e1cac018bc73","position":{"commit_sha":"1df42aae283d25bd8a1690985cce808b4b54b3ca","position":"1793915435570402001-5c57b26c-7682-49df-ad64-e1cac018bc73"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"11893c9e344cc297041eba646761f00a75ebd397a30a13febcb569f751955f0c","event_uuid":"d2275822-4afd-4102-961c-1a2ca2709ace","position":{"commit_sha":"3d1fd0d0438cd2ab96d39e18eceaa3b459eaf42b","position":"1793915444222141001-d2275822-4afd-4102-961c-1a2ca2709ace"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"58879ea27f38864471125e7754a8d114949ef1b787ef9e1fc2d8a8469ee3b675","event_uuid":"1fdf9fbf-079b-41a7-89c0-c64cd9553312","position":{"commit_sha":"6263117c3fbce5e92cb6e5f268ff47820c466b33","position":"1793915604232142001-1fdf9fbf-079b-41a7-89c0-c64cd9553312"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"5efdfab6bb4197f869cbbd7b40e8396e64ea35bc96fc6472e5652c9c06e053d5","event_uuid":"7bd00ed7-d280-4ceb-a604-b889c6e183e4","position":{"commit_sha":"2bcdad3d6a9eb7738f215e5066fe15e848ff4e52","position":"1793915615449246001-7bd00ed7-d280-4ceb-a604-b889c6e183e4"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"75a4810c9c4ec6c065b1307b35b87ef074a837eb5c506518349e699174c2ef8f","event_uuid":"68240966-605c-455d-94a2-6490b5c33e02","position":{"commit_sha":"125c665c98c30c071db057a3e2513f17b37d2bcc","position":"1793915632687414001-68240966-605c-455d-94a2-6490b5c33e02"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Design decision 2026-11-05 (operator): release syncs in BOTH directions between rebar and Jira fixVersions; both sides may edit, conflicts resolve like other bridged fields. Description updated accordingly.","timestamp":1793914378376475001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Design decision 2026-11-05 (operator): the release field is a LIST mirroring Jira fixVersions, add-wins like labels. Found: REB has 0 versions and its edit screen omits fixVersions (REB-7015 editmeta), so 2-way writes need a Jira admin step; recorded under 'Jira prerequisites'.","timestamp":1793914627147356001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Operator direction 2026-11-05: resolve the release list sync the way tags<->labels sync works (per-event add/remove delta with removals-before-additions replay, inbound set-diff applied as a delta with no-op suppression, outbound REMOVE gated by the local ever-seen intent set, per-item Jira add/remove update verbs). Recorded in the description's 'List sync follows the tags/labels pattern' section.","timestamp":1793914709737369001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Design decision 2026-11-05 (operator): rebar stores release NAMES on each ticket, exactly like tags; no release records. A Jira rename surfaces as remove+add on affected tickets; release status/dates stay in Jira.","timestamp":1793914850858496001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Design decision 2026-11-05 (operator): when a rebar ticket names a release the Jira project lacks, the bridge does not write it, keeps it on the rebar ticket, raises a BRIDGE_ALERT naming the missing version, and retries each pass. The bridge never creates Jira versions. Added an acceptance criterion.","timestamp":1793914957835308001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Design decision 2026-11-05 (operator): Jira 'Affects versions' (versions) is out of scope; only fixVersions syncs. All design questions are now settled and recorded in the description.","timestamp":1793915444222141001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Design decision 2026-11-05 (operator): no release inheritance through the parent hierarchy, mirroring Jira (Fix versions is Jira's release field for all work types and does not propagate from epic to children). A ticket's release is only what it stores; list --release X returns exactly those tickets.","timestamp":1793915615449246001}],"created_at":1793912050029097001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nTeams plan and ship work by release in Jira, using the issue field `fixVersions`. rebar has no release concept, so the bridge drops that field:\n- The bridge's field contract (`src/rebar/reconciler/_field_contract.py`) registers 11 fields; none is `fixVersions`.\n- Compiled ticket state (`src/rebar/reducer/_state.py`) has no release field.\n- No CLI, MCP or library surface can show, filter or set a release.\n\nSo rebar can't answer \"what is in release X?\" without Jira, and release membership is invisible to `next-batch`, `ready` and metrics.\n\n## Goal\n\nMake release a first-class rebar ticket field, synced both ways with Jira's `fixVersions` (Jira's release field for every work type) by the existing reconciler, and shown and filtered in `show`, `list` and the MCP tools.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. **ADR first.** Record the design under `docs/adr/`. It must cover:\n   - the field's shape;\n   - the replayed delta event that carries it (see the tags pattern below; not `EDIT.fields`, which replays last-writer-wins);\n   - its symmetry class in `FIELD_CONTRACT`;\n   - name-based identity and how renames surface;\n   - what happens when a Jira version is archived or deleted.\n2. **Store and reducer.** Add the field to compiled state with a default, and compact it into `SNAPSHOT`. Older stores replay unchanged, and older readers ignore the field under the schema forward-compatibility rules in `docs/event-schema.md`.\n3. **Reconciler.** Fetch and write `fixVersions` in both Jira adapters (Cloud and Data Center, via the `jira_family` seam, ADR 0055), inbound and outbound per the tags pattern below. Register the field in `FIELD_CONTRACT` and `conflict_resolver.FIELD_CLASSES`.\n4. **Surfaces.** `show`, `edit`, `list`/`search` filters and the MCP tools expose the field; `outputSchema`s and the public-API census are updated deliberately.\n5. **Docs.** `docs/event-schema.md`, `docs/ticket-model.md`, `docs/jira-sync-setup.md`, ADR 0121's field list.\n\n## List sync follows the tags/labels pattern (operator direction 2026-11-05)\n\n- **Storage and replay:** tags live as a list in compiled state and change through per-event deltas. `TAG_DELTA {added, removed}` is applied by `rebar.reducer._processors.process_tag_delta`: removals first, then additions, so an add beats a remove in the same event and replay is deterministic. Releases get the same delta shape. The ADR decides whether that is a new delta event or a generalized one; no whole-list EDIT writer.\n- **Inbound (Jira->rebar):** `inbound_collection_diffs._diff_labels_inbound` set-diffs Jira labels against local tags. `apply_inbound_events._inbound_update_apply_labels` writes a TAG_DELTA, reading current state only to suppress no-ops, and skips the write if the reducer fails rather than assuming an empty set. Inbound-origin events carry `source=inbound`.\n- **Outbound (rebar->Jira):** `outbound_labels._diff_labels` emits a REMOVE only for values in the local ever-seen intent set from `local_label_intent`. That set scans CREATE, EDIT, TAG_DELTA and SNAPSHOT and skips inbound-origin events (bug a06c), so a value Jira added and rebar never had is never removed from Jira.\n- **Jira writes:** labels change through per-item update verbs (`{\"update\":{\"labels\":[{\"add\"|\"remove\": ...}]}}`, Data Center `add_field_value` / `update(remove)`), never a whole-list set, so a concurrent Jira-side edit is not overwritten. `fixVersions` is an array field and should take the same add/remove update verbs. This is unverified against the live API, because REB's edit screen omits the field; the first child checks it.\n- **Contract:** `FIELD_CONTRACT` `add_wins`, conflict class `set`, with the property tests covering it as they cover labels.\n\n## Design decisions (all settled 2026-11-05; the ADR records them)\n\n- **Cardinality: DECIDED 2026-11-05 by the operator: a list of releases**, mirroring Jira's `fixVersions` (schema `{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":\"version\"}` on the live field API), with labels' add-wins rule.\n- **Direction: DECIDED 2026-11-05 by the operator: both directions.** rebar can set the release, the bridge writes it to Jira `fixVersions`, and Jira changes sync into rebar. Missing version (DECIDED 2026-11-05): the bridge does not write it; the release stays on the rebar ticket, a `BRIDGE_ALERT` names the missing version, and each pass retries until the version exists in Jira. The bridge never creates Jira versions.\n- **Entity: DECIDED 2026-11-05: names only, exactly like tags.** A Jira rename is a remove plus an add on each affected ticket; release details (released, date, archived) stay in Jira.\n- **Affects versions: DECIDED 2026-11-05: out of scope.** Jira's `versions` field is not synced; rebar has no affected-release field.\n\n- **Hierarchy: DECIDED 2026-11-05: no inheritance, mirroring Jira.** A ticket's release is only what it stores; `list --release X` returns exactly those tickets.\n\n## Jira prerequisites found 2026-11-05\n\n- REB defines 0 versions, and no issue on the site has a fix version set.\n- REB's edit screen does not expose `fixVersions`: the REB-7015 editmeta omits it. So rebar→Jira writes need a Jira admin to add Fix versions to REB's edit screen, and the versions must exist in the project. Versions are created in Jira by people, never by the bridge.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- **Portability.** Any or no CI provider; a store with no Jira bridge has the field empty and behaves as before.\n- **No config key.** A bridged project needs no new setting. The field syncs whenever the bridge runs. Any new mechanism needs a marker that names an open sunset ticket under this epic.\n- **Module size.** The 800-line cap, complexity ratchet and mechanism ratchet stay green. Split along existing seams; don't grow near-cap reconciler modules.\n- **No churn.** A first pass over an unchanged store writes only initial values; a repeat pass writes nothing.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] An ADR under `docs/adr/` records the field shape, event carrier, symmetry class, Jira version identity mapping, and archived/deleted version handling. It records each decision above.\n- [ ] Compiled ticket state carries the release field, with an empty default. `SNAPSHOT` compaction preserves it, and replaying an existing store unchanged yields an empty value for every ticket. Pinned by reducer and compaction tests.\n- [ ] A reconcile pass that sees a bridged Jira issue's `fixVersions` change writes the matching rebar event, and a rebar-side release change updates the Jira issue's `fixVersions`. A repeat pass with no change on either side writes nothing. Pinned for both the Jira Cloud and Data Center adapters by tests over recorded API payloads.\n- [ ] The field is registered in `FIELD_CONTRACT` and `conflict_resolver.FIELD_CLASSES`, and the contract property tests pass for it.\n- [ ] `rebar show` displays the field, `rebar edit` (and the MCP/library edit surfaces) can set it, and `rebar list` can filter by release. The MCP read tools return it in their declared `outputSchema`. Pinned by CLI, MCP and library tests.\n- [ ] `docs/event-schema.md`, `docs/ticket-model.md`, `docs/jira-sync-setup.md` and `docs/mcp-reference.md` describe the field. The doc-drift tests pass.\n- [ ] A rebar release naming a version the Jira project lacks is not written; the ticket gets a `BRIDGE_ALERT` naming it, each pass retries, and the alert resolves once the version exists. Pinned by tests.\n- [ ] A store with no Jira bridge passes the existing test suite unchanged.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0 on the final child's merge.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] On the production bridge, after deploy, one REB issue's fix version set in Jira appears on its bound rebar ticket after the next reconcile pass, and a release set on a rebar ticket appears on its Jira issue after the next pass. Shown with `rebar show` and the Jira issue view, and recorded in a ticket comment with the pass times.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"21ec-3e9b-4a27-4775","ticket_type":"epic","title":"Sync Jira fix versions into rebar as a first-class release field","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["6dc719bf-d232-44e9-bcb3-dcd5630b2a5d","7849ca9f-583d-48c8-bd15-e3c07c0d869d","558d7d7c-72df-44d4-b920-9d8c0dba69ef","f7598fc2-af63-4a11-bf9b-5bd06c8cff03","124d9df5-986e-44ee-ac35-4ec4e32eaed4","f10bf9ba-095a-4960-98b6-9f9799bc2d00","6024e7c3-c9ab-4dd3-883e-bfe3fbd1cea3","5cb68f1c-83d3-4fa7-9153-3ae6e3337e62","dd3fb164-cb4d-458a-9644-0623eaab17c6","48565745-61ea-40f1-90de-3a3ac5bda2fb","88dfa983-3716-4d68-97dc-0161dcf3461c","1d1126ad-bb79-419b-85e7-a73e080f70bc","78bcb008-8d5f-4562-a86d-199ac3315041","5c57b26c-7682-49df-ad64-e1cac018bc73","d2275822-4afd-4102-961c-1a2ca2709ace","1fdf9fbf-079b-41a7-89c0-c64cd9553312","7bd00ed7-d280-4ceb-a604-b889c6e183e4","68240966-605c-455d-94a2-6490b5c33e02"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793915632687414002,"uuid":"a3ede590-77a1-4f2e-a15c-aac666535bc9"}